From 0b5a058bb4c251d7845ea2179d75266dc5094514 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glenn Gore <glenn.g@affinidi.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:35:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add application contexts to Attest, Prove, VerifyAtt,
 VerifyProof and Issue

A deployment needs to bind an attestation to data the paper's contexts
do not carry: statement metadata, a validity window, a serial, and a
verifier challenge on the proof. This adds that binding as an
implementation note, without changing the paper's algorithms.

- attestation_context_with_app / issuance_context_with_app: the caller's
  bytes enter ctx_j and ctx_0 as framed items ("app", "att-app").
  With None they are byte-identical to the existing contexts, so every
  existing attestation and proof is unchanged.
- attest_in_context, check_attestation_in_context, prove_in_context,
  check_proof_in_context, issue_in_context. The trait of the ten
  algorithms is untouched.
- ctx_0 also binds each attestation's context, so a prover cannot check
  an attestation under one context and prove under another.
- Tags do not depend on the context: one attester for one id still
  counts once (DuplicateAttester).

tests/application_context.rs covers the round trip, the binding in every
direction, None vs Some(&[]), the count mismatch, context-independent
tags and byte-for-byte backward compatibility, for PS, BBS and EQ.

Signed-off-by: Glenn Gore <glenn.g@affinidi.com>
